!=========================================== This mechanism is the supplementary material to the work of
! Authors: Mengdi Li, Xiaoyu He*, Hamid Hashemi, Peter Glarborg, Vincent M. Lowe, Paul Marshall, Ravi Fernandes, Bo Shu*
! Title: An experimental and modeling study on auto-ignition kinetics of ammonia/methanol mixtures at intermediate temperature and high pressure
!
! *****************************************************************************
! *****************************************************************************
! ****************** For further documentation of mechanism:  *****************
! ****************** see references below and their citations *****************
! *****************************************************************************
! *****************************************************************************
!
! *****************************************************************************
!                          Nitrogen sub-mechanism                             *
! *****************************************************************************
!
! L. Dai, H. Hashemi, P. Glarborg, S. Gersen, P. Marshall, A. Mokhov, H. Levinsky,
! "Ignition delay times of NH3 /DME blends at high pressure and low DME fraction: RCM experiments and simulations",
! Combust. Flame. 227 (2021) 120–134.
!
! based on the review of Glarborg et al. below 
! P. Glarborg, J.A. Miller, B. Ruscic, S.J. Klippenstein,         
! "Modeling Nitrogen Chemistry in Combustion",                    
! Prog. Energy Combust. Sci. 67 (2018) 31-68.
!
! Dai adopted the theoretical rate constants for some reactions from below
! A. Stagni, C. Cavallotti, S. Arunthanayothin, Y. Song, O. Herbinet, F. Battin-Leclerc, T. Faravelli,
! "An experimental, theoretical and kinetic-modeling study of the gas-phase oxidation of ammonia",   
! React. Chem. Eng. 5 (2020) 696–711.
! 
! and adopted the theoretical rate constants for some reactions from below
! X. Chen, M.E. Fuller, C. Franklin Goldsmith,
! "Decomposition kinetics for HONO and HNO2",
! React. Chem. Eng. 4 (2019) 323–333.
!
! *****************************************************************************
!                           methanol sub-mechanism                             *
! *****************************************************************************
!
! U. Burke, W.K. Metcalfe, S.M. Burke, K.A. Heufer, P. Dagaut, H.J. Curran,
! "A detailed chemical kinetic modeling, ignition delay time and jet-stirred reactor study of methanol oxidation"
! Combust. Flame. 165 (2016) 125–136.
!
! based on the AramcoMech 1.3 by Burke et al.
! W.K. Metcalfe, S.M. Burke, S.S. Ahmed, H.J. Curran,
! "A Hierarchical and Comparative Kinetic Modeling Study of C1 − C2 Hydrocarbon and Oxygenated Fuels"
! Int. J. Chem. Kinet. 45 (2013) 638–675.
!
! including the H2/CO/O2 reactions of Kéromnès et al.
! A. Kéromnès, W.K. Metcalfe, K.A. Heufer, N. Donohoe, A.K. Das, C.-J. Sung, J. Herzler, C. Naumann, P. Griebel, O. Mathieu, M.C. Krejci, E.L. Petersen, W.J. Pitz, H.J. Curran
! "An experimental and detailed chemical kinetic modeling study of hydrogen and syngas mixture oxidation at elevated pressures"
! Combust. Flame. 160 (2013) 995–1011.
!
! including the C1-C4 reactions of Metcalfe et al. 
! W.K. Metcalfe, S.M. Burke, S.S. Ahmed, H.J. Curran
! "A Hierarchical and Comparative Kinetic Modeling Study of C1 − C2 Hydrocarbon and Oxygenated Fuels"
! Int. J. Chem. Kinet. 45 (2013) 638–675.
!
! other adopted rate constant of reactions can be found in the kinetic modeling part.

!
! *****************************************************************************
!                    NH3/CH3OH (ammonia/methanol) subset                      *
! ***************************************************************************** 
!
! Mengdi Li, Xiaoyu He, Hamid Hashemi, Peter Glarborg, Vincent M. Lowe, Paul Marshall, Ravi Fernandes, Bo Shu
! "An experimental and modeling study on auto-ignition kinetics of ammonia/methanol mixtures at intermediate temperature and high pressure"
!
ELEMENTS
C
H
N
O
AR
HE
END
